  "notes": "DRAFT 2026-10-12 from https://www.bankofamerica.com/credit-cards/products/cash-back-credit-card/ and https://www.bankofamerica.com/credit-cards/products/cash-back-credit-card/cash-back-category-choices/ (issuer pages, read directly; the product page showed a 'temporarily unavailable' banner but the rewards text rendered). Needs human review. User picks ONE of six categories (gas/EV, online shopping, dining, travel, drug stores, home improvement); only one choice-category rule should apply at a time; can be changed once per calendar month. 3% rate shown is the post-first-year rate; new accounts earn 6% in the choice category for the first year (3% + 3% first-year bonus) and 6%/2% apply on the first $2,500 combined purchases each quarter. First-year 6% is not modeled. The $2,500 cap is QUARTERLY and COMBINED across the choice category and grocery/wholesale, then 1%; cap_usd omitted because the engine field is annual. Not modeled: online shopping (incl. cable, internet, phone, streaming), home improvement and furnishings, $200 online bonus offer, BofA Rewards (Preferred Rewards) bonus. Travel category also covers parking, transit, taxis/rideshare; car rental not explicitly named so not mapped. Merchant MCC assignment can exclude some purchases. Wholesale clubs are grouped with groceries here."
